mpleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5.beta5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6119) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n<img width=\"401\" height=\"478\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0766114f-2802-4f6d-b397-999232c4311e\" />\n\nWhen creating a curve for Curve Angle, it is set with -360 and 360 as min and max respectively. It seems to me that those values are read as radians rather than as degrees by the ParticleProcessMaterial.\n\nWhen I use a min/max of -3.14 and 3.14, I can easily control the results (e.g. 1 turn, 1/2 turn, etc). \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a GPUParticle\nCreate a Particle Process Material\nSet a draw pass\nCancel the gravity\nCreate a Angle Curve\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nDefault Project","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"